invariant: INV-14
file: quic_config.c
catches: quic_loop_host
reason: ch_quic_init of a host object stops asking for the caller's
  description of its CPU, so a QUIC client stages a ClientHello for a
  configuration that never set ch_cfg.cpu. The server's rule in srv.c is
  untouched, so only the client's row notices: test/quic_loop_cpu.h
  requires CH_EINVAL and a failed session for 0.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    // The caller's description of its CPU (cpu_cfg.h), before any rule
    // that reads it.
    if (!cpu_bits_ok(cfg)) {
        return CH_EINVAL;
    }
#endif
--- new
